        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::VbFile::makeDumpHeader</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Makes the header for a dumped *vb.txt* file :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

An element&apos;s ``SemanticIndex`` is its occurrence among the elements sharing its
:cpp:func:`BufType::getName` -- so the first ``TEXCOORD`` is index 0, the next is 1,
which is how 3dmigoto tells several same-named elements apart
</verbatim></para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>The header text, ending with the <computeroutput>vertex-data:</computeroutput> marker the data section follows </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/model/files/VbFile.h" line="75" column="25" bodyfile="src/model/files/VbFile.cpp" bodystart="68" bodyend="102"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_vb_file_1a2c74a6558cc95631c3626c500048ef2f" prot="public" static="no" const="yes" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::string</type>
        <definition>std::string AGRemapCore::VbFile::getDumpStr</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;prefix=&quot;vb0&quot;) const</argsstring>
        <name>getDumpStr</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::VbFile::getDumpStr</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>prefix</declname>
          <defval>&quot;vb0&quot;</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The full text for converting this ``.vb`` file into a dumped *vb.txt* file --
#makeDumpHeader followed by :cpp:func:`BufFile::getDumpStr`&apos;s data section
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. warning::
   This deliberately **hides** :cpp:func:`BufFile::getDumpStr` rather than overriding
   it -- that one is documented as returning only the data section, and code holding a
   plain :cpp:class:`BufFile` should keep getting exactly that
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>prefix</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The buffer name each entry is prefixed with</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The text for the dumped <emphasis>vb.txt</emphasis> file </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/model/files/VbFile.h" line="94" column="25" bodyfile="src/model/files/VbFile.cpp" bodystart="104" bodyend="109"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_vb_file_1a18a10cc98d900636326d48c1138e4b9c" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void AGRemapCore::VbFile::readDumpStr</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;text)</argsstring>
        <name>readDumpStr</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::VbFile::readDumpStr</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>text</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Reads a dumped *vb.txt* file&apos;s text back into this file&apos;s bytes -- the inverse of
#getDumpStr :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Unlike :cpp:func:`BufFile::readDumpStr`, which encodes against whatever #getElements the
file already has, this first rebuilds those elements from the dump&apos;s own header (see
#parseDumpHeader) when there is one -- so a dump can be read straight back without
being told its layout. A header-less text falls through to the current elements
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>text</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The text of the dumped <emphasis>vb.txt</emphasis> file</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>BadBufData</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if the parsed bytes do not divide evenly into vertex lines </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/model/files/VbFile.h" line="112" column="18" bodyfile="src/model/files/VbFile.cpp" bodystart="111" bodyend="118"/>
